File description

The repository keeps the pattern files (*.axx) in patfile/ and the assembly
sources (*.s, with the .tsv files they import) in asmsrc/. In a flat working
directory they all sit side by side; test1 and the scripts accept either
layout. Below, the files are listed by directory and then by subject.

"test1 compares ..." means test1 assembles the pair with both caxx and paxx
and compares the results with cmp.

```
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Top level: the implementations and building
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
axx.py                              axx in Python, 'Paxx': the reference
                                    implementation; new features land here
                                    first
caxx.c                              axx in C, 'Caxx': the same output byte for
                                    byte, with its own 256-bit integer type
                                    (uint256_t)
faxx.fs                             axx in Forth, 'Faxx': the entry for gforth
                                    (gforth faxx.fs <pattern> <source> ...);
                                    loads faxxsrc/load.fs and runs main
faxxsrc/                            the sources of Faxx (69 files, listed at
                                    the end of this file)
build_ccforth.sh                    compiles Faxx with ccforth (Forth -> C)
                                    and a C compiler into the executable faxx,
                                    which takes the same arguments as
                                    gforth faxx.fs. CCFORTH / CC / CFLAGS /
                                    MEMSIZE / KEEPC tune it
makefile                            make: caxx and paxx (and axx, a copy of
                                    axx.py); make faxx: faxx; make all: all
                                    three; make install: caxx, paxx, faxx and
                                    the man page
test1                               the assemble test: every pattern file /
                                    source pair through caxx and paxx, the
                                    results compared with cmp (also -o, -g,
                                    -v, -V and the diagnostics)
secsort.py                          rewrites a source so that its lines are
                                    grouped by section (.section ...
                                    .endsection), following .include
axx.1.gz                            axx man page
.gitignore                          the build products, test1's a<n> / b<n>
                                    outputs and other leftovers

