patfile/: pattern files for the ELF output (-o)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
elftype.axx                         .elftype: a relocation type name defined
                                    in the pattern file, written in .reloc and
                                    in the source's .extern / .global (manual
                                    3.7.6)
elfgen.axx                          the ELF description directives
                                    .elfmachine / .elfclass / .elfrela /
                                    .elfwidth / .elfextern / .elfdwarf /
                                    .elfheader: the whole ELF machine
                                    description of EM_MSP430, a machine axx
                                    has no built-in table for (manual 3.7.7)
elfprio.axx                         the relocation type priority: the default
                                    guessed from the field width, then the
                                    pattern file's .reloc, then the source's
                                    ::<type>, each beating the one before
                                    (manual 3.7.8)
elfpair.axx                         relocations that come in pairs or with a
                                    companion, section groups and sh_link, on
                                    RISC-V (riscv64.axx is included):
                                    .elfextra adds R_RISCV_RELAX to every
                                    call, .elfdiff writes sums and differences
                                    of labels as ADD / SUB pairs (also a
                                    ULEB128 and a 6-bit field, and the
                                    advances of a relaxed .eh_frame),
                                    .elfgroup makes a COMDAT group and
                                    .elflink sets the sh_link of a link-order
                                    section (manual 3.7.10)
elfcfi.axx                          call frame information: the source's
                                    .cfi_* directives become an .eh_frame;
                                    .elfcfi / .elfcfiinit / .elfcfireg
                                    describe the CIE and the DWARF register
                                    numbers (x86-64, manual 3.7.11)
elfmips.axx                         .elfencode: MIPS32 (REL) whose R_MIPS_HI16
                                    field is written back by a mini-language
                                    function ((addend+0x8000)>>16), with
                                    R_MIPS_26 and R_MIPS_LO16 through
                                    .elffield (manual 3.7.10)
elfmips64.axx                       .elfrinfo: MIPS64 (n64, little-endian),
                                    whose r_info puts the type in the top
                                    byte; a mini-language function lays it out
                                    (manual 3.7.10)
elfword.axx                         .elfunit: a toy machine with 16-bit words
                                    whose addends and symbol values are
                                    counted in words (manual 3.7.10)
elfsec.axx                          .elfsection: the sh_flags, sh_type and
                                    sh_addralign of a section whose name axx
                                    has no rule for -- a vector table, an
                                    uninitialised region not called .bss, a
                                    note section, and a section whose
                                    alignment is written out (manual 3.7.7)
elfsym.axx                          the pieces that make the output a linkable
                                    .o for any CPU: the ELF symbol attributes
                                    of the source (.type / .size / .weak /
                                    .hidden / .protected / .internal / .other
                                    / .comm, manual 5.6.1), a relocation field
                                    width that is not a power of two
                                    (.elfwidth::3) and a section element size
                                    (the fifth field of .elfsection). the
                                    machine is EM_MN10300, which axx has no
                                    built-in table for
elfrel.axx                          a REL machine whose relocations live in
                                    instruction fields: ARM (EM_ARM) described
                                    with .elfbuiltin::0, so no built-in table
                                    is used, and the shift and bias fields of
                                    .elffield that put the addend back into
                                    the instruction (manual 3.7.7, 3.7.9)

