patfile/: translators (.textmode, -V)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
intel2att.axx                       translates x86-64 Intel syntax source into
                                    AT&T syntax source text: .textmode with
                                    `!Y` symbol captures for the register and
                                    mnemonic sets, `!L` captures so labels and
                                    expressions keep the spelling they had in
                                    the input, and the macro layer (`!def` /
                                    `!while`) to generate the 28
                                    memory-operand shapes for every operand
                                    size. swaps the operand order, adds `%` to
                                    registers and `$` to immediates, rewrites
                                    [base+index*scale+disp] as
                                    disp(%base,%index,scale), and derives the
                                    b / w / l / q suffix (manual 3.18)
8080toz80.axx                       translates Intel 8080 source into Zilog
                                    Z80 source text: .textmode, `!L` captures
                                    and `{{.exp()}}`, so labels and
                                    expressions keep the spelling they had in
                                    the input (manual 3.18)
a64tox64_axx.axx                    translates AArch64 assembly into x86_64
                                    assembly in the notation of x86_64.axx:
                                    register mapping, calling-convention glue
                                    and syscall remapping via a small runtime
                                    (a64rt_axx*.s). the translated
                                    bf_aarch64.s runs mandelbrot.bf (manual
                                    3.18)

